1️⃣ [@madara.ternovaja|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U02K91QUK6V] reviewed the process and confirmed that it won't be too much struggle for her to document our process in a clear way 🚀 

2️⃣ These are the following changes I made based on the comments from the PEX team:
{{Main process}}

* Added [+a note+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=194-647&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4] that highlights that the agent needs to address and solve *all the issues* mentioned by the customer;
* Removed the need to check T&C while researching for info from [+here+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=113-609&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4] as several PEX members mentioned that it would be too much;
* Enhanced the [+duplicate tickets check process+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=82-339&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4];
* Changed the wording from *_educating_* to *_informing_* [+here+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=113-839&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4] as education sounds like the customer did something wrong and it's not what we mean;
* Moved [+documenting the case in internal notes step+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=196-827&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4] to the end of the process (now it goes after replying to the customer);
* Added [+a step to check Linked cases+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=172-654&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4] on Beehive but for now we're not sure what the agent should do afterwards we decided I should observe how the agents are handling these tickets and work it out from there.

{{Customer reopens a ticket after it was closed}}

* Added [+a step to double check if the solution was correct+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=196-1012&t=jmC1fEKVxdzN2kdw-4].

3️⃣ I mapped the existing 🌍 [+Information about automatic compensations+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/13270?country=global&language=en] process and I'm in the process of making a [+to-be map+|https://www.figma.com/board/Z7dTZTQtFBHLOg1fOm8cxE/Non-safety-ticket-handling-process?node-id=203-1420&t=12zn49YfeISnRN6n-4]. It's not finished yet as I need to clarify couple of things.

Marharyta from the T&W team also shared [+this spreadsheet+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eIZdh9n5WVyy-z3fgEMZn9hBaTUKcju1AZ_2Och5E2g/edit?gid=2053048568#gid=2053048568] with me that can give us insight into the logic they use to create automations. I feel like she is not that willing to change anything 😅 I'll try to ask more follow-up questions, but I doubt I'll be successful in my negotiations.

Since automation compensates the user once or twice in 30 days, it seems like our logic is that we are willing to spend money for when the comp is not even needed to retain the customer

4️⃣ In order to make sure that the future process covers everything the agent needs, me and Asia decided that it would be a great exercise for me to *jump on a call with a CS agent and observe the way they solve tickets*. I will have one session with a RH agent tomorrow and another with a Food agent on Thursday. I will note all my observations and see whether I need to modify or update the existing process maps.

5️⃣ Regarding calls - communication with Fred [+here+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04LU7CDY49/p1728029507931449], TLDR is that if we want agents to offer calls we need to make sure that they are able to handle *all kinds of cases*. At the moment it's not possible, because we don't have a secure way to verify users via the call, and Privacy is waiting for the Product team to confirm if they can work on creating this secure verification process. More on this [+here+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04UPSKM561/p1728543026711849].

