{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
_“I note from the DSA that the personal data that is being shared here is the name, contact details and tier of Romanian drivers -_ {color:#4c9aff}*_is this correct_*{color}_? If so,_ {color:#4c9aff}*_in what direction is this data being shared, and by who_*{color}_?”_
{panel}

*Response*: Yes, this is correct. Most probably we will need from Eurolife the name, contact details of Romanian drivers that complete Eurolife required form in order to obtain the discounted insurance. We don’t have a clear process here, yet.

*Thoughts*: The DSA mentions name, contact details and tier. {color:#ff5630}Ask the business to confirm if tier will be transferred - if not, this can be removed{color}. 

Also, Bolt is listed as the data exporter - {color:#ff5630}this is not correct{color}. This raised the following issues:

* Roles of parties in Annex 1 need to be switched around. Some of the obligations say that the data importer is the company, which it is not.
* The DSA places a lot of obligations on Bolt, rather than the counterparty. These are not necessarily overly burdensome, but they are another stick to beat Bolt with.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
{color:#4c9aff}*_“Is the counterparty also based in Romania_*{color}_? Additionally, do we know if the counterparty will be transferring the personal data at-issue onwards to other third parties?”_
{panel}

*Response*: Yes. The counter party is also based in Romania. I can ask if the personal data at-issue will be transferred to other third part parties and come back with an answer.

*Thoughts*: {color:#ff5630}Get business to confirm this point{color}, as the DSA notes that restricted transfers are not taking place.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
_“Can we_ {color:#4c9aff}*_fix the numbering of the clauses_*{color} _in the DSA so that they are continuous?”_
{panel}

*Response*: I think [~accountid:712020:9f38c9c2-43a9-46c6-9106-86ff0d35ba24] is the most fitted to make adjustments to the file.

*Thoughts*: This is not on me. However, {color:#ff5630}numbering still not resolved{color} - this may create contractual confusion and is an easy fix.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
“Finally,{color:#4c9aff} *how will these discounts be presented to drivers*{color} - will they just be presented on a general ‘Bolt Rewards’ page, or will drivers be specifically messaged about the discounts?”
{panel}

*Response*: The discounts will be presented in the Bolt Rewards page. From Bolt Rewards page driver will be redirected to a specific page for each insurance type where he/she will have to complete a form with several details so that he can receive a quotation for the insurance.

*Thoughts*: Does not sound like direct electronic marketing to users. Also, sounds like the counterparty will actually be collecting the data at-issue in the first instance, and then providing it to Bolt.

