{quote}Maybe spend half a day on research and trying?{quote}

I have tested on a dev kit that USB suspend - resume indeed works if I do changes to esp-idf code. A more general question if we do want to introduce changes to esp-idf or fork it somwhow.


{quote}Is there a chance that newer esp-idf versions add support without hacking?{quote}

I have posted a question to Espressif forum

Another problem that the remote wakeup is not possible if the modem is connected using PPP or ECM, meaning that you can put the modem into sleep mode but it won’t be able to signal to the host if new data has arrived. The host would need to periodically wakeup the modem to check for new data. This would either make sleep cycles very short or introduce a large latency when renting a scooter. The reply from Quectel:

{quote}You can get URC only if you use TCP AT commands. So +QIURC: "recv" for example will wake up the host on incoming TCP/UDP data. But it is related to internal TCP stack and its AT commands. It will not work when PPP or ECM are used. 

Also, incoming voice call or SMS will wake up the host, as there will be URC also.  {quote}

So my current understanding that in order to make the modem sleep mode useful we need to:

# Make changes to esp-idf to support USB suspend-resume or use UART
# Connect modem ring pin (in case of USB connection)
# USE TCP AT commands as a primary mean to send and receive data from the modem

