PSP returns {{card.do-not-honor}} error. It is usually a generic error. When issuers don’t categorize errors they return this error code. We map this error to {{PAYMENT_ERROR_TEMPORARY}} error, which is correct. Sometimes it makes sense to retry.

RefundV2 endpoint in the payment core service doesn’t have a special [handler|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment_core/main/controller/router/RefundControllerV2.ts#L97] for this error code and hence it converts it to {{PROVIDER_REFUND_FAILED}}

{noformat}if (refundAction.state === PaymentRowState.ERROR) {
    if (refundAction.errorCode === PaymentResponseCodes.PAYMENT_ERROR_PERMANENT) {
        return RefundResults.error(
            RefundErrorCodes.REFUND_FAILED_PERMANENTLY,
            "Provider refund not retriable",
        );
    }
    throw new PaymentRouterError(PaymentRouterErrors.PROVIDER_REFUND_FAILED, "Refund action failed", {
        paymentAttempt,
        error: {code: refundAction.errorCode, message: refundAction.errorMessage},
    });
}{noformat}

[Then|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment_core/main/controller/router/RefundControllerV2.ts#L47] it converts it to SERVER_ERROR and writes to logs {{Refund failed with unmapped error code}} and throws an exception with SERVER_ERROR code.

{noformat}} catch (e) {
    const {code, message, meta} = ExceptionHelper.parse(e);
    if (code === ResponseCodes.CLIENT_TIMEOUT) {
        logger.info(ctx, "Refund timeout error", {...meta, request, hint: message});
        throw e;
    }
    if (
        [ResponseCodes.INVALID_REQUEST, ResponseCodes.DATABASE_ERROR, ResponseCodes.SERVER_ERROR].includes(code)
    ) {
        logger.error(ctx, "Refund error", {...meta, request, hint: message});
        throw e;
    }

    logger.error(ctx, "Refund failed with unmapped error code", {...meta, request, hint: message});
    throw BoltError.code(ResponseCodes.SERVER_ERROR, message, e);
}{noformat}

Balance user service for all errors thrown like exceptions do re-tries.

At the end, we reach the threshold of retries and mark the payment as {{bolt.payops-required}} Which means that manual work from Payments Ops is required. 

