The total count query takes too much time on prelive.

{code:json}{
  "duration": 60005,
  "query": "/* ROUTE READONLY=1 */\n/* identity-verification-process-76c486c57f-qzxdz|@verification|identity-verification-process|external|/adminPanel/scheduledForDataDeletion/list|prelive-identityverificationprocess */\nSELECT /*+ MAX_EXECUTION_TIME(59991) */ COUNT(*) as count\n            FROM `flow_run_scheduled_data_deletion` AS frsdd\n                JOIN `flow_run` AS fr ON fr.id = frsdd.flow_run_id\n            WHERE frsdd.status IN ('scheduled') AND frsdd.delete_after > FROM_UNIXTIME(1729548000)\n        ",
  "warning_limit": 1000
}{code}

{code:sql}SELECT COUNT(*) as count
  FROM `flow_run_scheduled_data_deletion` AS frsdd
    JOIN `flow_run` AS fr ON fr.id = frsdd.flow_run_id
  WHERE frsdd.status IN ('done') AND frsdd.delete_after > FROM_UNIXTIME(1729548000){code}

In this particular request we may omit the {{JOIN}} part, which speeds up the query up to 0.3s.
Also, the {{delete_after_status_idx}} index is suboptimal for this query.

{code:sql}  INDEX `delete_after_status_idx` (`delete_after` ASC, `status` ASC),{code}

{noformat}id|select_type|table|partitions|type |possible_keys          |key                    |key_len|ref|rows  |filtered|Extra                   |
--+-----------+-----+----------+-----+-----------------------+-----------------------+-------+---+------+--------+------------------------+
 1|SIMPLE     |frsdd|          |range|delete_after_status_idx|delete_after_status_idx|4      |   |337745|    25.0|Using where; Using index|{noformat}

A more efficient index would be

{code:sql}INDEX `delete_after_status_idx` (`status` ASC, `delete_after` ASC),{code}

where the {{status}} column goes first.

