Hey [~accountid:5cefa65be2e3ec0fc196de31]! Thanks for your concerns & questions!

Let me try to clarify the situation: the business client we’re talking about is [Nova Post|https://novapost.com/] - the 3rd biggest company in UA with 40,000+ employees. This is an extremely important deal for Bolt Business in UA, which we’ve been working on for almost 2 years to close. They currently runrate to be doing ~72,000 rides p.a. and that’s considering we have not even fully onboarded them yet.

They have a ton of branches across Ukraine and with the current situation with war & curfews, we, unfortunately, can’t meet their demands in supply in select locations. In some regions with local ops we have created custom high-surge polygons to stimulate the drivers, in others even that is not an option. They do not want to have several providers for transportation and the dissatisfaction is piling up resulting in a significant risk of losing the client.

The fact that a handful of their employees volunteered to help other employees with commute is actually a gift from above to us, since there is nothing else we can do to help them really.

*Answering your Qs:*

{color:#0747a6}_Would you have an estimation, how likely such a scenario will be happening with another company/another supply?_{color}

Not likely. It’s not something that we are offering to clients. It’s an exception.

{color:#0747a6}_Will this setup be gaining popularity in the business space?_ {color}

No.

{color:#0747a6}_How many, on average, new drivers are added to such a scenario as supply per week/month?_{color}

This is not a regular practice, so hard to tell. Right now we have 8 drivers (7 in Odesa and 1 in Zhytomyr) who do this. I do not expect the total number to go over 20 in the future.

{color:#0747a6}_I am correct to assume these drivers will also be rejecting any orders from other (not-this-business) orders if these get offered?_{color}

They only go online when they need give rides to their colleagues, so yes, generally they do not take orders outside of this arrangement. Although it’s not like we’re prohibiting them from taking other orders if they want some extra money on the side - up to them I guess.

{color:#0747a6}_Have these drivers gone through generic onboarding and training to be eligible for other orders? What would be the restriction for them not to service other customers? Are there any servicing other customers?_{color}

They went through exactly the same registration/training process as any other individual driver in UA - submitted all docs, etc. Literally no difference.

{color:#0747a6}_Hence, we would need some kind of a flag, tag, category, company or group for the exclusive drivers._{color}

Do you have a way to quickly tag drivers without needing us to create a separate fleet? We’re talking about a handful drivers here and, in all honesty, outside of the fact that they are serving one client mostly, they are not a separate fleet really. If you can create a ‘Nova Post’ tag or smth, and quickly tag them that would be fine.

{color:#0747a6}_Would you know, what would be the stoppers here to align or assign these drivers under one company/entity?_{color}

They really are not under one company (as drivers) - they are separate individual sole proprietors doing the rides, helping out their colleagues. We just want them to not get banned constantly for taking orders from the same people.

Thanks!

